brcmfmac: fall back to legacy MBSS when interface_create is unsupported

Pre-2016 FullMAC firmwares (e.g. BCM43602 fw 7.35.177.56 on the Netgear R8000)
do not implement the modern "interface_create" iovar. request_ap_if() tries it,
then queries the supported version, and on query failure returns -EOPNOTSUPP,
skipping the legacy "bsscfg:ssid" MBSS fallback right below that this firmware
does support. Result: a 2nd AP BSS fails with add_iface -95 even though MBSS is
detected. Fall through to the legacy path instead of bailing.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c
@@ -726,4 +726,4 @@
 	if (err) {
 		brcmf_err("fail to get supported version, err=%d\n", err);
-		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
+		iface_create_ver = 0; /* R8000: fall through to legacy mbss */
 	}
